UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Not such an easy hand to play. Nicely done. Having said that, if West remembered that East led the @C9 then West, at trick six. could have played the @C8 rather than the @CJ on the second club. Then the hand would be down 1. But it is often hard to keep track of the spots below the 10.|
PG| ***** 35 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|There were several possible lines. One would be to not draw any trump and try and cross ruff, though I am not sure that comes to enough tricks  because you have to lose the lead at least once when you lead a diamond.|
PG| ***** 36 ***** |


