%%%% Hand 4
https://tinyurl.com/26tov5qf
qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4|pn|hondo717,Honeydog3,mcannon,cfrleon|
md|3S842HAKQT94DA52C3,SKQJ3H7D9843CQT86,ST5H32DQJT76C9752,SA976HJ865DKCAKJ4|sv|n|
mb|P|mb|1C|mb|1H|mb|D|mb|P|mb|1S?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I have 7 likely tricks. But I am vulnerable. So I would consider bidding 3@H, and that could work out well particularly since they have an 8 card spade fit. You may ask how do I know they have an 8 card fit?|
PG| ***** 57 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Well, West made a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=negativedoubles,Negative Double^*N|CP||FP||at| showing exactly 4 spades and East opened 1@C and should only have 4 spades except in the rare instance (such as on Board 1) where East is 5-6.|
PG| ***** 58 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Per |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| they should be in 2@S when West gets to bid. So I will risk 3@H to make it hard for them.
|
PG| ***** 59 ***** |


mb|3H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now let me discuss something called a ^*BMaximal Double^*n which is very useful here. Play that, if West bids 3@S that is to play. But if West wants to invite, can double. I am not sure what I would do with the West hand even playing ^*BMaximal Doubles^*n.|
PG| ***** 60 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BEast: ^*NIf West doubles what are my options?|
PG| ***** 61 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East can bid 3@S with a minimum hand and 4@S with a maximum hand. With East hand I would bid 4@S over the double by West. However, on this auction not clear what East should do.|
PG| ***** 62 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Personally in this bidding cycle, I would pass--very unclear--and I would have made a ^*BMaximal Double^*n with the West hand because of the singleton heart. ^*UBut who knows^*N. That is why I bid 3@H to make it difficult for the opponents.|
PG| ***** 63 ***** |


mb|P|mb|3S|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 64 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|HQ|pc|H7|pc|H3|pc|H5|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The expert lead from AKQ is the Q. Once it wins then partner knows you have the AK as well.|
